{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelResummation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelResummation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Normed","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.abs_borelTransformValue_le_of_gevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.abs_borelTransformValue_le_of_gevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L302-L322","doc":"**Quantitative disc bound**: the Borel value of a Gevrey-1 sequence is\nbounded by `C/(1 − A·|z|)` on the disc. (The exponential-type control that\nfeeds the Laplace-integrability step of the resummation half.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformValue_eq_tsum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformValue_eq_tsum","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L292-L300","doc":"Under summability, the class-chosen Borel value IS the sum of the\nBorel-transformed series. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformConverges_of_gevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformConverges_of_gevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L284-L290","doc":"**Every Gevrey-1 sequence has a convergent Borel transform on its disc**\n(`A·|z| < 1`) — hypothesis half (i) of Nevanlinna–Sokal, sorry-free, as a\nproducer of `BorelTransformConverges` instances. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransform_tendsto_tsum_of_gevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransform_tendsto_tsum_of_gevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L274-L282","doc":"The partial Borel transforms of a Gevrey-1 sequence converge on the disc,\nto the sum of the Borel-transformed series. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.summable_borel_of_gevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.summable_borel_of_gevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L268-L272","doc":"Gevrey-1 ⇒ summability of the Borel-transformed series itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.summable_abs_borel_of_gevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.summable_abs_borel_of_gevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L258-L266","doc":"**Gevrey-1 ⇒ absolute summability** of the Borel-transformed series on the\ndisc `A·|z| < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.abs_borelCoeff_mul_pow_le_of_gevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.abs_borelCoeff_mul_pow_le_of_gevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L246-L256","doc":"Term-wise geometric domination of the Borel-transformed series on the\ndisc: `|(aₙ/n!)·zⁿ| ≤ C·(A·|z|)ⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.abs_borelCoeff_le_of_gevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.abs_borelCoeff_le_of_gevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L236-L244","doc":"**Borel division turns a Gevrey-1 bound into a geometric one**: the Borel\ncoefficients of a Gevrey-1 sequence are bounded by `C·Aⁿ`. This is the\ngeneral form of `borel_tames_factorial`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.gevrey1_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.gevrey1_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L231-L234","doc":"The factorial series is Gevrey-1 with `C = A = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.Gevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.Gevrey1","kind":"def","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L226-L229","doc":"Gevrey-1 (factorial-type) bound: `|aₙ| ≤ C·Aⁿ·n!` — the hypothesis class\nof the Nevanlinna–Sokal theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformValue_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformValue_smul","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L197-L202","doc":"**The Borel-transform value is homogeneous** — the scalar leg of linearity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.instBorelTransformConverges_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.instBorelTransformConverges_smul","kind":"instance","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L189-L195","doc":"**The convergence class is closed under scalar multiplication.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.partialBorel_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.partialBorel_smul","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L181-L187","doc":"The partial Borel transform is homogeneous in the source sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelCoeff_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelCoeff_smul","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L176-L179","doc":"Borel coefficients are homogeneous under scalar multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformValue_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformValue_add","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L167-L174","doc":"**The Borel-transform value is additive** — linearity at the limit level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.instBorelTransformConverges_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.instBorelTransformConverges_add","kind":"instance","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L157-L165","doc":"**The convergence class is closed under addition.** If the Borel transforms\nof `a` and `b` both converge at `z`, so does the transform of `a + b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.partialBorel_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.partialBorel_add","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L149-L155","doc":"The partial Borel transform is additive in the source sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformValue_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformValue_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L134-L141","doc":"The Borel-transform value of the factorial series is `(1 − z)⁻¹` on the\nunit disc, confirming `borelTransformValue` computes the geometric sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.instBorelTransformConverges_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.instBorelTransformConverges_factorial","kind":"instance","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L128-L132","doc":"The factorial series `Σ n! zⁿ` has a convergent Borel transform on the unit\ndisc — a nonvacuous instance of the conditional class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransform_factorial_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransform_factorial_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L111-L126","doc":"**The conditional class is genuinely inhabited** — a sorry-free witness.\nThe Borel transform of the series `Σ n! zⁿ` (radius of convergence `0`;\ndivergent for every `z ≠ 0`) is the geometric series `Σ zⁿ`, which\nconverges on `|z| < 1` to `(1 − z)⁻¹`. This is the concrete analytic\ncontent that pins `BorelTransformConverges` down to a real convergence\nstatement (as opposed to an empty marker): the partial Borel transforms\nof the factorial series tend to `(1 − z)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransform_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransform_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L105-L109","doc":"The Borel transform indeed converges to `borelTransformValue`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelTransformValue","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L100-L103","doc":"The Borel-transform value at `z` (the limit), available once\n`[BorelTransformConverges a z]` is supplied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelTransformConverges.converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelTransformConverges.converges","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L97-L97","doc":"the partial Borel transforms converge to some limit at `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelTransformConverges.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelTransformConverges.mk","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelTransformConverges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelTransformConverges","kind":"class","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L88-L98","doc":"**Borel-transform convergence** — the first half of Borel summability, with\ngenuine content: the partial Borel transforms `Σ_{n≤N}(aₙ/n!)zⁿ` converge as\n`N → ∞` to `value`. (The *second* half — the Laplace resummation\n`∫₀^∞ e^{−t} φ(z t) dt` and Watson / Nevanlinna–Sokal UNIQUENESS — is the\nsubstantial analysis NOT yet in Mathlib; it is documented in the file\nheader as the gap, deliberately not stated with measure-theory imports\nabsent from the cache, and NEVER `sorry`-faked.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelCoeff_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelCoeff_add","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L83-L86","doc":"Borel coefficients are linear in the source sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.partialBorel_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.partialBorel_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L75-L81","doc":"Consequently the partial Borel transform of `Σ n! zⁿ` is the geometric\npartial sum `Σ_{n=0}^{N} tⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borel_tames_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borel_tames_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L67-L73","doc":"**The Borel mechanism: division by n! tames factorial divergence.**\nThe (everywhere-divergent) series `Σ n! zⁿ` has unit Borel coefficients —\nits Borel transform is the geometric series `Σ tⁿ = 1/(1−t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.partialBorel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.partialBorel","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L63-L65","doc":"The partial Borel transform `Σ_{n=0}^{N} (aₙ/n!) tⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.borelCoeff","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelResummation.lean#L60-L61","doc":"The Borel transform coefficient of a formal series `Σ aₙ zⁿ`: `aₙ / n!`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}